## TURN BUDGET (all backends)

This session's rollover target is ~{{ turn_soft_cap }} agent/tool turns. Claude,
Grok, and current Google Gemini CLI versions use native turn limits; Gemini
also keeps a completed-tool fallback for older versions. Codex and OpenCode
stop after completed tool events. Antigravity (`agy`) exposes neither a native
cap nor a stable completed-tool event contract, so it must follow the target
cooperatively and remains wall-clock bounded.

Checkpoint every conclusion to structured state as soon as it is known. In the
last quarter of the budget, finish the current hypothesis and save its outcome
rather than opening a new one. A newly filed crash gets a bounded enrichment
tail where the CLI permits one; otherwise the next resume presents it ahead of
all other work.

`TURN_SOFT_CAP=0` disables rollover. Do not attempt to override the operator's
setting from inside the session.
